WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.631
Welcome to ChainPilot.

2
00:00:01.631 --> 00:00:06.015
In this video you'll see how to install it, set up your plan,

3
00:00:06.015 --> 00:00:09.105
subscribe with MTN MoMo, and run a session.

4
00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:14.926
You'll also see exactly how the compounding strategy works, and what it can't do.

5
00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:17.815
Start on the ChainPilot website.

6
00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:20.961
Open the download page and get the installer.

7
00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:27.184
You need Windows 10 or 11, and Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge, which comes with Windows.

8
00:00:27.838 --> 00:00:32.569
Because the installer is new, Windows may say it protected your PC.

9
00:00:32.569 --> 00:00:34.899
Click More info, then Run anyway.

10
00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:41.325
ChainPilot installs for your Windows account only, so it doesn't need administrator rights.

11
00:00:41.981 --> 00:00:46.093
When setup finishes, open ChainPilot from the Start menu.

12
00:00:46.093 --> 00:00:52.080
The control panel opens in its own window, and a small log window starts minimised.

13
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.604
Keep it open while ChainPilot runs.

14
00:00:55.259 --> 00:01:00.527
The first time, ChainPilot asks you to confirm that you are 18 or older,

15
00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.235
and that you understand what it does.

16
00:01:03.235 --> 00:01:07.479
It doesn't predict rounds, and it doesn't change the odds.

17
00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:10.186
On average, every bet loses about 3%.

18
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.357
Accept, and you're in.

19
00:01:12.357 --> 00:01:17.390
There are four tabs: Play, How compounding works, Subscription, and Help.

20
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:21.182
The badge on the right shows whether you're subscribed.

21
00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.126
Your plan lives on the Play tab.

22
00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:25.631
First, choose a mode.

23
00:01:25.631 --> 00:01:29.069
A dry run watches real rounds and bets on paper.

24
00:01:29.069 --> 00:01:32.723
Practice clicks for real, on the game's play money.

25
00:01:32.723 --> 00:01:33.726
Both are free.

26
00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:37.093
Live uses real money, and needs a subscription.

27
00:01:37.746 --> 00:01:41.105
The initial bet is what every chain starts with.

28
00:01:41.105 --> 00:01:44.604
If a chain is lost, this is exactly what it costs.

29
00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.583
We'll use ten.

30
00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.266
Cash out at is your multiplier.

31
00:01:48.266 --> 00:01:51.477
ChainPilot turns on the game's own Auto Cash Out,

32
00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:55.212
so the game's server takes the win at exactly this point.

33
00:01:55.212 --> 00:01:56.720
There's no click delay.

34
00:01:57.372 --> 00:02:00.186
Wins per chain is where compounding happens.

35
00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:03.831
After each win, the whole payout rides on the next round,

36
00:02:03.831 --> 00:02:06.965
until this many wins in a row complete the chain.

37
00:02:07.618 --> 00:02:08.999
Then come your limits.

38
00:02:08.999 --> 00:02:13.206
Stop after ends the session when you've completed this many chains.

39
00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:17.726
The loss limit stops the session before its loss could pass this amount.

40
00:02:17.726 --> 00:02:20.175
Set it to money you can afford to lose.

41
00:02:20.175 --> 00:02:21.556
We'll use one hundred.

42
00:02:21.556 --> 00:02:25.637
And the time limit ends the session after the minutes you choose.

43
00:02:26.291 --> 00:02:30.649
Rounds between bets waits a random number of rounds after each bet.

44
00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:32.926
It spreads your bets out over time.

45
00:02:32.926 --> 00:02:34.682
It doesn't change the odds.

46
00:02:35.335 --> 00:02:45.522
As you type, "This plan at a glance" shows what your settings mean: what a full chain pays, how likely it is, and the average return.

47
00:02:45.522 --> 00:02:49.505
With these settings, a full chain turns 10 into 247.

48
00:02:49.505 --> 00:02:52.875
60, but only about 1 chain in 29 gets there.

49
00:02:53.527 --> 00:02:55.209
Here's the idea.

50
00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:58.256
You bet 10, cashing out at 1.

51
00:02:58.256 --> 00:02:58.677
90×.

52
00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:04.247
A win pays 19, and all of it rides on the next round.

53
00:03:04.247 --> 00:03:05.088
Then 36.

54
00:03:05.088 --> 00:03:05.823
10, 68.

55
00:03:05.823 --> 00:03:06.664
59, 130.

56
00:03:06.664 --> 00:03:06.979
32.

57
00:03:06.979 --> 00:03:10.763
Five wins in a row turn 10 into 247.

58
00:03:10.763 --> 00:03:11.078
60.

59
00:03:11.732 --> 00:03:14.034
But one loss anywhere ends the chain.

60
00:03:14.034 --> 00:03:18.763
You lose your ten, because everything above it was the chain's own winnings.

61
00:03:18.763 --> 00:03:21.190
Then a new chain starts again from ten.

62
00:03:21.843 --> 00:03:27.233
The catch is that the chance shrinks as fast as the stake grows.

63
00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:27.654
At 1.

64
00:03:27.654 --> 00:03:31.023
90×, one bet wins about 51% of the time.

65
00:03:31.023 --> 00:03:36.582
Each step needs another win, so five in a row happen only about 3.

66
00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:37.845
5% of the time.

67
00:03:37.845 --> 00:03:40.288
That's roughly 1 chain in 29.

68
00:03:40.941 --> 00:03:43.361
And the house edge compounds too.

69
00:03:43.361 --> 00:03:46.734
On average the game returns 97% of what's bet.

70
00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:53.626
A five-step chain is five bets riding on each other, so it returns about 86% of its first bet.

71
00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:56.486
Compounding makes the rare wins bigger.

72
00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:59.932
It doesn't change which way the average points.

73
00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:05.758
You can check all of this with your own numbers, on the How compounding works tab.

74
00:04:05.758 --> 00:04:10.457
The story at the top describes your chain, and the tiles show the key odds.

75
00:04:11.118 --> 00:04:15.552
The ladder shows every step: what you bet, what it pays if it wins,

76
00:04:15.552 --> 00:04:18.464
and the chance that the chain gets that far.

77
00:04:19.119 --> 00:04:21.957
Try a lower multiplier, and fewer steps.

78
00:04:21.957 --> 00:04:26.144
Chains now complete far more often, but they pay much less.

79
00:04:26.144 --> 00:04:29.124
The average return per bet doesn't change.

80
00:04:29.778 --> 00:04:34.579
Back on our original plan, ChainPilot simulates 4,000 sessions below.

81
00:04:34.579 --> 00:04:39.797
Most sessions end down, usually at the loss limit, and some reach the goal.

82
00:04:39.797 --> 00:04:42.649
That's the honest shape of this strategy.

83
00:04:43.302 --> 00:04:48.553
When you're happy with a plan, press Use these settings, to copy it to the Play tab.

84
00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:51.564
Live betting needs a subscription.

85
00:04:51.564 --> 00:04:53.367
Open the Subscription tab.

86
00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.795
This is your computer's machine ID.

87
00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.361
Your subscription belongs to this PC.

88
00:04:59.012 --> 00:05:02.803
Choose a plan, then enter your MTN MoMo number.

89
00:05:03.456 --> 00:05:04.822
Press Pay with MoMo.

90
00:05:04.822 --> 00:05:07.486
A payment prompt arrives on your phone.

91
00:05:07.486 --> 00:05:11.039
Check the amount, and approve it with your MoMo PIN.

92
00:05:11.691 --> 00:05:15.670
As soon as MoMo confirms, ChainPilot activates by itself.

93
00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:20.906
If you renew early, the new days are added to the end of your subscription.

94
00:05:21.559 --> 00:05:26.331
Reinstalled Windows, or closed the app before the payment confirmed?

95
00:05:26.331 --> 00:05:27.945
Press Restore purchase.

96
00:05:27.945 --> 00:05:30.612
You can also paste a license key here.

97
00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:36.230
Back on the Play tab, open the game window, and log in to the casino there.

98
00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.348
ChainPilot remembers your login.

99
00:05:38.348 --> 00:05:41.593
Keep that window open and visible while it plays.

100
00:05:42.245 --> 00:05:43.803
Let's start a dry run.

101
00:05:43.803 --> 00:05:46.636
In this video, the rounds are simulated.

102
00:05:46.636 --> 00:05:52.584
In real use, ChainPilot plays in the game window, with the game's own Auto Cash Out.

103
00:05:53.237 --> 00:05:58.695
The session panel shows the running total, how many bets won, completed chains,

104
00:05:58.695 --> 00:05:59.870
and the next bet.

105
00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:04.913
Every bet is listed below, and saved to a spreadsheet you can open later.

106
00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.076
Press Stop at any time.

107
00:06:07.076 --> 00:06:10.955
A bet that's already in the air is allowed to settle first.

108
00:06:10.955 --> 00:06:15.887
For live betting, ChainPilot asks you to confirm before it bets real money.

109
00:06:16.538 --> 00:06:21.530
The Help tab has a quick guide, links to support services, your bet logs,

110
00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.172
and a check for updates.

111
00:06:23.172 --> 00:06:27.959
Fixes for the game page download automatically when ChainPilot starts.

112
00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:34.115
Before every session, set a loss limit you can afford to lose, and a time limit.

113
00:06:34.115 --> 00:06:36.798
Never raise your limit to chase losses.

114
00:06:36.798 --> 00:06:41.133
If gambling stops being fun, take a break, and talk to someone.

115
00:06:41.787 --> 00:06:43.064
That's ChainPilot.

116
00:06:43.064 --> 00:06:47.960
Download it for free, try the simulator, a dry run and practice mode,

117
00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.940
and subscribe with MoMo when you're ready.

118
00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.920
Thanks for watching, and play responsibly.
